and the completion's own echo are.

THE PROBE, and why it is one arm and not the batch. The thrust's premise was "a baseline WITH HEADROOM", and
the correction above withdrew it: the 60% it rested on was measured on the 35B through this id. The premise is
now UNMEASURED on the real 27B, and it is the single fact that decides whether the 48-run batch is worth
running on this cell. So it gets its own arm first, at a quarter of the cost.

WHAT RUNS: one arm, N=12, cell 17-realguide-envserver-deltaassert, the SHIPPED tool files (write_file.py
f858ee38e993, edit.py e92a8bdfa39c), the ADR-0176 prompt (b57bdb96285b) deployed for the arm and the standing
ADR-0180 prompt (302a7becd55b) restored after it, the bench tree's own loop.py (07d461afa424), temperature 0,
--no-pin, sequential, model id zds-qwen3.8-27b, requests dumped. This is the batch script's (a1) arm and its
bookends, nothing else; the registered t36_batch.sh (2d5b46d830a3) is not modified and not used. The runner is
repointed from the host NAME to the fleet's canonical tailnet address for the pod -- the literal lives in the
fleet's own convention, not in this public log -- which is what every other fleet caller now uses, and it takes
a name-resolution dependency out of a long run.

THE READING RULE, enumerated over all thirteen possible outcomes of a 12-run arm, fixed before the arm runs.
Let P be the number of runs that pass the cell's verifier.
  P = 11 or 12  -> CEILING. Cell 17 cannot show an improvement on this model: a rule line has at most one run
                  of room, which is the defect that voided thrust 35's second sample. Thrust 36 does not launch
                  on this cell; the cell choice is reopened and re-registered.
  P = 2 to 10   -> HEADROOM. The premise holds in the form the thrust needs. Thrust 36 is re-registered with P
                  as its baseline, new predictions derived from P, and then the interleaved batch launches.
  P = 0 or 1    -> FLOOR. The cell fails on this model for reasons a write-tool rule line does not address, so
                  a treatment effect could not be separated from the noise of everything else failing. Thrust
                  36 does not launch on this cell; the cell choice is reopened and re-registered.
SECOND SAMPLE, fixed now so it cannot be chosen after seeing the number: if P lands within one of a boundary
(P = 0, 1, 2, 10, 11 or 12) a SECOND arm of 12 runs under identical conditions and the pooled 24 is read on the
same proportions -- pooled >= 22 CEILING, 4 to 21 HEADROOM, <= 3 FLOOR. Any other P is read on the first arm
alone. A run that errors out counts as a MISS, as in every arm of this campaign.

DESCRIBED, NEVER PART OF THE RULE: turns and elapsed per run, the pass pattern across the twelve, and from the
dumps the number of runs that open the sibling test file (the registration's "about 23%" sibling-read route is
a 35B number too and is not a prediction here). Decode speed is reported because it sets every future arm's
wall time: the 27B is expected around 10.7 tok/s decode against the 35B's 43.66, so an arm that took about 7
minutes will take substantially longer, and a slow FIRST turn after an engine restart is a cold prefill and not
a hang.

WHAT NO OUTCOME LICENSES. Any comparison with a pre-2026-08-22 27B number: that lane ran a different
